{{also|trick or treat}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From the phrase stated as a greeting when accosting a household, "Trick or Treat!". From the activity of threatening a trick to receive a treat.

===Verb===
{{en-verb|head=[[trick]]-[[or]]-[[treat]]}}

# To [[extort]] small treats on [[Halloween]] by implied threat of property damage or [[practical joke]].

